Activity 5: Guide Questions
1. What do all the methods (move(), special_move(), use()) in the previous activities have in common?

They all have the same purpose of performing an action, but each class gives the method its own behavior.

2. How does this activity show polymorphism in a gaming context?

It shows polymorphism because different game characters and items can use the same method name but perform different actions or have different effects.

3. Can you think of other examples where the same action behaves differently depending on the character or item?

One example is an attack() method. A warrior can attack using a sword, a mage can attack using magic, and an archer can attack using a bow.
